# The browser the image installs, pinned.
#
# The browser is the one component whose version decides what the agent sees:
# the operator viewport broke between two builds of the same commit because
# Debian's security channel moved chromium from 153 to 154 in between. Nothing
# here rolls with the distribution any more.
#
# Every build path reads this file and passes the three values as build
# arguments (./build.sh, .github/workflows/build.yml, both jobs of e2e.yml), the
# Dockerfile refuses to build without them, and the smoke job compares the
# browser inside the published image against `upstream` below.
#
# Chromium and chromium-common come from the same source and are installed
# together, at the same version, so apt cannot pair a pinned chromium with a
# chromium-common from another build. Patch versions carry the distribution
# revision: 154.0.8037.57-1~deb12u1 is the Debian package version, while
# `chromium --version` prints 154.0.8037.57.
#
# Raising the pin is deliberate: change the versions here, rebuild, and let the
# end to end suite decide. The build fails on its own, loudly, the day the
# distribution drops the pinned version from its channel.
chromium_package=154.0.8037.57-1~deb12u1
chromium_common=154.0.8037.57-1~deb12u1
chromium_upstream=154.0.8037.57
